IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `pip-nouns`
IMPORT `pip-dates`
IMPORT `pip-part3-required-period`

-- PART 6 -- PROVISIONS RELATING TO AGE: regulations 25 to 27.
--
-- Layer 1: the law, objectively. Section 83(1) of the Act stops personal independence payment for a person who has
-- reached the relevant age; these regulations say when it does not apply. The relevant age is the Act's term and the
-- fact that C has reached it is an input.
-- out of text: Welfare Reform Act 2012 s 83

§ `Regulation 25: exceptions to section 83 where entitlement exists or claim made before the relevant age`

-- reg 25: section 83(1) of the Act does not apply where C has reached the relevant age if C (a) was entitled to an
-- award of either or both components on the day preceding the day on which C reached the relevant age; or (b) made a
-- claim for personal independence payment before reaching the relevant age and that claim was not determined before C
-- reached that age but an award of either or both components would be made in respect of C but for section 83(1) of the Act.
-- src:360 | 25 Exceptions to section 83 where entitlement exists or claim made before relevant age
-- src:361 | Section 83(1) of the Act (persons of pensionable age) does not apply where C has reached the relevant age if C —
-- src:362 | (a) was entitled to an award of either or both components on the day preceding the day on which C reached the relevant age; or
-- src:363 | (b) made a claim for personal independence payment before reaching the relevant age and that claim was not determined before C reached that age but an award of either or both components would be made in respect of C but for section 83(1) of the Act.
@ref reg 25(b) (src:363)
GIVEN `C made a claim for personal independence payment before reaching the relevant age` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that claim was not determined before C reached that age` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an award of either or both components would be made in respect of C but for section 83(1) of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 25(b): the claim made before the relevant age qualifies` MEANS
        `C made a claim for personal independence payment before reaching the relevant age`
    AND `that claim was not determined before C reached that age`
    AND `an award of either or both components would be made in respect of C but for section 83(1) of the Act`

@ref reg 25 (src:361-363)
GIVEN `C has reached the relevant age` IS A BOOLEAN
      `C was entitled to an award of either or both components on the day preceding the day on which C reached the relevant age` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claim made before the relevant age qualifies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 25: section 83(1) of the Act does not apply to C` MEANS
        `C has reached the relevant age`
    AND `reg 25: one of the two exceptions applies` `C was entitled to an award of either or both components on the day preceding the day on which C reached the relevant age` `or` `the claim made before the relevant age qualifies`

GIVEN a IS A BOOLEAN
      b IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 25: one of the two exceptions applies` a `or` b MEANS
    a OR b

§ `Regulation 26: claim after an interval and after reaching the relevant age`

-- reg 26(1): where C has reached the relevant age and makes a new claim in the circumstances set out in regulation 15 the
-- following exceptions apply.
-- src:364 | 26 Claim for personal independence payment after an interval and after reaching the relevant age
-- src:365 | (1) Where C has reached the relevant age and makes a new claim in the circumstances set out in regulation 15 the following exceptions apply.
@ref reg 26(1) (src:365)
GIVEN `C has reached the relevant age` IS A BOOLEAN
      `C makes a new claim in the circumstances set out in regulation 15` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 26(1): the exceptions of regulation 26(2) apply` MEANS
        `C has reached the relevant age`
    AND `C makes a new claim in the circumstances set out in regulation 15`

-- reg 26(2)(a): section 83(1) of the Act does not apply.
-- src:366 | (2) The exceptions referred to in paragraph (1) are—
-- src:367 | (a) section 83(1) of the Act (persons of pensionable age) does not apply;
@ref reg 26(2)(a) (src:367)
GIVEN `the exceptions of regulation 26(2) apply` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 26(2)(a): section 83(1) of the Act does not apply to C` MEANS
    `the exceptions of regulation 26(2) apply`

-- reg 26(2)(b): the reference to "2 years" in regulation 15(1)(b) is to be read as "1 year". The result is the number of
-- years that regulation 15(1) takes as its input.
-- src:368 | (b) the reference to ‘2 years’ in regulation 15(1)(b) is to be read as ‘1 year’;
@ref reg 26(2)(b) (src:368)
GIVEN `the exceptions of regulation 26(2) apply` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`reg 26(2)(b): the number of years in regulation 15(1)(b)` MEANS
    IF `the exceptions of regulation 26(2) apply` THEN 1 ELSE `reg 15(1)(b): the number of years`

-- reg 26(2)(c) and (d): the rate of the mobility component C is entitled to on the new claim, from the level assessed on
-- the new claim and the rate C was entitled to under the previous award of personal independence payment or adult
-- disability payment. (c) Severely limited ability: the enhanced rate only if C was entitled to that rate under the
-- previous award, and otherwise the standard rate if C was entitled to that rate under it. (d) Limited ability: the
-- standard rate only if C was entitled to the component, at either rate, under the previous award. Where regulation 26(1)
-- does not apply these paragraphs say nothing: NOTHING. A level of neither gives no rate.
-- src:369 | (c) where C is assessed as having severely limited ability to carry out mobility activities for the purposes of the new claim—
-- src:370 | (i) C is entitled to the enhanced rate of the mobility component only if C was entitled to that rate of that component under the previous award of personal independence payment or adult disability payment; and
-- src:371 | (ii) where C is not entitled to the enhanced rate of that component because of paragraph (i), C is entitled to the standard rate of that component provided that C was entitled to that rate of that component under the previous award of personal independence payment or adult disability payment; and
-- src:372 | (d) where C is assessed as having limited ability to carry out mobility activities for the purposes of the new claim, C is entitled to the standard rate of the mobility component only if C was entitled to that component, at either rate, under the previous award of personal independence payment or adult disability payment.
@ref reg 26(2)(c), reg 26(2)(d) (src:369-372)
GIVEN `the exceptions of regulation 26(2) apply` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the level of ability to carry out mobility activities assessed for the new claim` IS A `a level of ability to carry out activities`
      `the rate of the mobility component C was entitled to under the previous award` IS A `a rate of a component`
GIVETH A MAYBE `a rate of a component`
`reg 26(2)(c) and (d): the rate of the mobility component C is entitled to on the new claim` MEANS
    IF NOT `the exceptions of regulation 26(2) apply`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST (`reg 26(2)(c) and (d): the rate allowed` `the level of ability to carry out mobility activities assessed for the new claim` `the rate of the mobility component C was entitled to under the previous award`)

GIVEN level IS A `a level of ability to carry out activities`
      previous IS A `a rate of a component`
GIVETH A `a rate of a component`
`reg 26(2)(c) and (d): the rate allowed` level previous MEANS
    CONSIDER level
    WHEN `severely limited ability` THEN previous
    WHEN `limited ability` THEN
        IF previous EQUALS `no rate of the component`
        THEN `no rate of the component`
        ELSE `the standard rate of the component`
    WHEN `neither limited ability nor severely limited ability` THEN `no rate of the component`

§ `Regulation 26A: claim after Scottish adult disability living allowance and after reaching the relevant age`

-- reg 26A(1): where C has reached the relevant age and makes a new claim in the circumstances set out in regulation 15B(1)
-- the following exceptions apply.
-- src:373 | 26A Claim for personal independence payment after an award of Scottish adult disability living allowance and after reaching the relevant age
-- src:374 | (1) Where C has reached the relevant age and makes a new claim in the circumstances set out in regulation 15B(1) the following exceptions apply.
-- src:375 | (2) The exceptions referred to in paragraph (1) are—
@ref reg 26A(1) (src:374)
GIVEN `C has reached the relevant age` IS A BOOLEAN
      `C makes a new claim in the circumstances set out in regulation 15B(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 26A(1): the exceptions of regulation 26A(2) apply` MEANS
        `C has reached the relevant age`
    AND `C makes a new claim in the circumstances set out in regulation 15B(1)`

-- reg 26A(2)(a): section 83(1) of the Act does not apply.
-- src:376 | (a) section 83(1) of the Act (persons of pensionable age) does not apply;
@ref reg 26A(2)(a) (src:376)
GIVEN `the exceptions of regulation 26A(2) apply` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 26A(2)(a): section 83(1) of the Act does not apply to C` MEANS
    `the exceptions of regulation 26A(2) apply`

-- reg 26A(2)(b): the reference to "2 years" in regulation 15B(1)(b) is to be read as "1 year".
-- src:377 | (b) the reference to ‘2 years’ in regulation 15B(1)(b) is to be read as ‘1 year’.
@ref reg 26A(2)(b) (src:377)
GIVEN `the exceptions of regulation 26A(2) apply` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`reg 26A(2)(b): the number of years in regulation 15B(1)(b)` MEANS
    IF `the exceptions of regulation 26A(2) apply` THEN 1 ELSE `reg 15B(1)(b): the number of years`

§ `Regulation 27: revision and supersession of an award after the person has reached the relevant age`

-- reg 27(1): subject to paragraph (2), section 83(1) of the Act does not apply where (a) C has reached the relevant age
-- and is entitled to an award ("the original award") of either or both components pursuant to an exception in regulation
-- 25 or 26; and (b) that award falls to be revised or superseded.
-- src:378 | 27 Revision and supersession of an award after the person has reached the relevant age
-- src:379 | (1) Subject to paragraph (2), section 83(1) of the Act (persons of pensionable age) does not apply where —
-- src:380 | (a) C has reached the relevant age and is entitled to an award (“the original award”) of either or both components pursuant to an exception in regulation 25 or 26; and
-- src:381 | (b) that award falls to be revised or superseded.
@ref reg 27(1) (src:379-381)
GIVEN `C has reached the relevant age` IS A BOOLEAN
      `C is entitled to an award of either or both components pursuant to an exception in regulation 25 or 26` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that award falls to be revised or superseded` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 27(1): section 83(1) of the Act does not apply on the revision or supersession` MEANS
        `C has reached the relevant age`
    AND `C is entitled to an award of either or both components pursuant to an exception in regulation 25 or 26`
    AND `that award falls to be revised or superseded`

-- A date that is after the day C reached the relevant age; where there is no date the answer is no.
GIVEN d IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day C reached the relevant age` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 27(2): the date is after the day C reached the relevant age` d `than` `the day C reached the relevant age` MEANS
    CONSIDER d
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST x THEN x GREATER THAN `the day C reached the relevant age`

-- reg 27(2), first version (src:382-387): where the original award includes an award of the mobility component and is
-- superseded (a) pursuant to regulation 23 of the Decisions and Appeals Regulations for a relevant change of circumstances
-- which occurred after C reached the relevant age; or (b) pursuant to regulation 26(1)(a) of the Decisions and Appeals
-- Regulations where (i) the application for supersession was made by C after C reached the relevant age, or (ii) the
-- supersession proceedings were initiated by the Scottish Ministers after C reached the relevant age, the restrictions in
-- paragraph (3) apply in relation to the supersession.
-- The text has paragraph (2) twice (fork F-32); the second version names the Secretary of State.
-- src:382 | (2) Where the original award includes an award of the mobility component and is superseded—
-- src:383 | (a) pursuant to regulation 23 of the Decisions and Appeals Regulations for a relevant change of circumstances which occurred after C reached the relevant age; or
-- src:384 | (b) pursuant to regulation 26(1)(a) of the Decisions and Appeals Regulations where—
-- src:385 | (i) the application for supersession was made by C after C reached the relevant age, or
-- src:386 | (ii) the supersession proceedings were initiated by the Scottish Ministers after C reached the relevant age,
-- src:387 | the restrictions in paragraph (3) apply in relation to the supersession.
@ref reg 27(2) (first version) (src:382-387)
GIVEN `the original award includes an award of the mobility component` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the award is superseded pursuant to regulation 23 of the Decisions and Appeals Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date of the relevant change of circumstances` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the award is superseded pursuant to regulation 26(1)(a) of the Decisions and Appeals Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day C applied for supersession, if C did` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day the Scottish Ministers initiated the supersession proceedings, if they did` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day C reached the relevant age` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 27(2) (Scottish Ministers version): the restrictions in paragraph (3) apply` MEANS
        `the original award includes an award of the mobility component`
    AND `reg 27(2) (Scottish Ministers version): the supersession is within (a) or (b)`
            `the award is superseded pursuant to regulation 23 of the Decisions and Appeals Regulations`
            `the date of the relevant change of circumstances`
            `the award is superseded pursuant to regulation 26(1)(a) of the Decisions and Appeals Regulations`
            `the day C applied for supersession, if C did`
            `the day the Scottish Ministers initiated the supersession proceedings, if they did`
            `the day C reached the relevant age`

GIVEN `the award is superseded pursuant to regulation 23 of the Decisions and Appeals Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date of the relevant change of circumstances` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the award is superseded pursuant to regulation 26(1)(a) of the Decisions and Appeals Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day C applied for supersession, if C did` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day the Scottish Ministers initiated the supersession proceedings, if they did` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day C reached the relevant age` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 27(2) (Scottish Ministers version): the supersession is within (a) or (b)` MEANS
       `reg 27(2)(a): the supersession is for a change of circumstances after the relevant age`
           `the award is superseded pursuant to regulation 23 of the Decisions and Appeals Regulations`
           `the date of the relevant change of circumstances`
           `the day C reached the relevant age`
    OR (    `the award is superseded pursuant to regulation 26(1)(a) of the Decisions and Appeals Regulations`
        AND (   `reg 27(2): the date is after the day C reached the relevant age` `the day C applied for supersession, if C did` `than` `the day C reached the relevant age`
             OR `reg 27(2): the date is after the day C reached the relevant age` `the day the Scottish Ministers initiated the supersession proceedings, if they did` `than` `the day C reached the relevant age`))

GIVEN `the award is superseded pursuant to regulation 23 of the Decisions and Appeals Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date of the relevant change of circumstances` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day C reached the relevant age` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 27(2)(a): the supersession is for a change of circumstances after the relevant age` `the award is superseded pursuant to regulation 23 of the Decisions and Appeals Regulations` `the date of the relevant change of circumstances` `the day C reached the relevant age` MEANS
        `the award is superseded pursuant to regulation 23 of the Decisions and Appeals Regulations`
    AND `reg 27(2): the date is after the day C reached the relevant age` `the date of the relevant change of circumstances` `than` `the day C reached the relevant age`

-- reg 27(2), second version (src:388-393): the same with "the Secretary of State" in (b)(ii).
-- src:388 | (2) Where the original award includes an award of the mobility component and is superseded—
-- src:389 | (a) pursuant to regulation 23 of the Decisions and Appeals Regulations for a relevant change of circumstances which occurred after C reached the relevant age; or
-- src:390 | (b) pursuant to regulation 26(1)(a) of the Decisions and Appeals Regulations, where—
-- src:391 | (i) the application for supersession was made by C after C reached the relevant age, or
-- src:392 | (ii) the supersession proceedings were initiated by the Secretary of State after C reached the relevant age,
-- src:393 | the restrictions in paragraph (3) apply in relation to the supersession.
@ref reg 27(2) (second version) (src:388-393)
GIVEN `the original award includes an award of the mobility component` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the award is superseded pursuant to regulation 23 of the Decisions and Appeals Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date of the relevant change of circumstances` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the award is superseded pursuant to regulation 26(1)(a) of the Decisions and Appeals Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day C applied for supersession, if C did` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day the Secretary of State initiated the supersession proceedings, if they did` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day C reached the relevant age` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 27(2) (Secretary of State version): the restrictions in paragraph (3) apply` MEANS
        `the original award includes an award of the mobility component`
    AND `reg 27(2) (Secretary of State version): the supersession is within (a) or (b)`
            `the award is superseded pursuant to regulation 23 of the Decisions and Appeals Regulations`
            `the date of the relevant change of circumstances`
            `the award is superseded pursuant to regulation 26(1)(a) of the Decisions and Appeals Regulations`
            `the day C applied for supersession, if C did`
            `the day the Secretary of State initiated the supersession proceedings, if they did`
            `the day C reached the relevant age`

GIVEN `the award is superseded pursuant to regulation 23 of the Decisions and Appeals Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date of the relevant change of circumstances` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the award is superseded pursuant to regulation 26(1)(a) of the Decisions and Appeals Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day C applied for supersession, if C did` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day the Secretary of State initiated the supersession proceedings, if they did` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day C reached the relevant age` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 27(2) (Secretary of State version): the supersession is within (a) or (b)` MEANS
       `reg 27(2)(a): the supersession is for a change of circumstances after the relevant age`
           `the award is superseded pursuant to regulation 23 of the Decisions and Appeals Regulations`
           `the date of the relevant change of circumstances`
           `the day C reached the relevant age`
    OR (    `the award is superseded pursuant to regulation 26(1)(a) of the Decisions and Appeals Regulations`
        AND (   `reg 27(2): the date is after the day C reached the relevant age` `the day C applied for supersession, if C did` `than` `the day C reached the relevant age`
             OR `reg 27(2): the date is after the day C reached the relevant age` `the day the Secretary of State initiated the supersession proceedings, if they did` `than` `the day C reached the relevant age`))

-- reg 27(2A): "the Decisions and Appeals Regulations" means the Universal Credit, Personal Independence Payment,
-- Jobseeker's Allowance and Employment and Support Allowance (Decisions and Appeals) Regulations 2013.
-- src:394 | (2A) In paragraph (2), “the Decisions and Appeals Regulations” means the Universal Credit, Personal Independence Payment, Jobseeker’s Allowance and Employment and Support Allowance (Decisions and Appeals) Regulations 2013.
@ref reg 27(2A) (src:394)
`reg 27(2A): the Decisions and Appeals Regulations` MEANS
    "the Universal Credit, Personal Independence Payment, Jobseeker's Allowance and Employment and Support Allowance (Decisions and Appeals) Regulations 2013"

-- reg 27(3): the restrictions. (a) Where the original mobility component award is for the standard rate then, regardless of
-- whether the award would otherwise have been for the enhanced rate, the Secretary of State (i) may only make an award for
-- the standard rate of that component; and (ii) may only make such an award where entitlement results from substantially
-- the same condition or conditions for which the mobility component in the original award was made. (b) Where the original
-- mobility component award is for the enhanced rate, the Secretary of State may only award that rate of that component where
-- entitlement results from substantially the same condition or conditions. For a standard rate award on an original enhanced
-- award the text says nothing: NOTHING (fork F-33).
-- src:395 | (3) The restrictions referred to in paragraph (2) are —
-- src:396 | (a) where the original mobility component award is for the standard rate then, regardless of whether the award would otherwise have been for the enhanced rate, the Secretary of State -
-- src:397 | (i) may only make an award for the standard rate of that component; and
-- src:398 | (ii) may only make such an award where entitlement results from substantially the same condition or conditions for which the mobility component in the original award was made.
-- src:399 | (b) where the original mobility component award is for the enhanced rate, the Secretary of State may only award that rate of that component where entitlement results from substantially the same condition or conditions for which the mobility award was made.
@ref reg 27(3) (src:395-399)
GIVEN original IS A `a rate of a component`
      proposed IS A `a rate of a component`
      `entitlement results from substantially the same condition or conditions for which the mobility component in the original award was made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 27(3): the Secretary of State may award this rate of the mobility component` original `to replace` proposed `with` `entitlement results from substantially the same condition or conditions for which the mobility component in the original award was made` MEANS
    CONSIDER original
    WHEN `the standard rate of the component` THEN
        CONSIDER proposed
        WHEN `the standard rate of the component` THEN JUST `entitlement results from substantially the same condition or conditions for which the mobility component in the original award was made`
        WHEN `the enhanced rate of the component` THEN JUST FALSE
        WHEN `no rate of the component` THEN NOTHING
    WHEN `the enhanced rate of the component` THEN
        CONSIDER proposed
        WHEN `the enhanced rate of the component` THEN JUST `entitlement results from substantially the same condition or conditions for which the mobility component in the original award was made`
        WHEN `the standard rate of the component` THEN NOTHING
        WHEN `no rate of the component` THEN NOTHING
    WHEN `no rate of the component` THEN NOTHING

-- reg 27(4): where the original award does not include an award of the mobility component but C had a previous award of that
-- component, for the purpose of this regulation entitlement under that previous award is to be treated as if it were under the
-- original award provided that the entitlement under the previous award ceased no more than 1 year prior to the date on which
-- the supersession takes or would take effect.
-- src:400 | (4) Where the original award does not include an award of the mobility component but C had a previous award of that component, for the purpose of this regulation entitlement under that previous award is to be treated as if it were under the original award provided that the entitlement under the previous award ceased no more than 1 year prior to the date on which the supersession takes or would take effect.
@ref reg 27(4) (src:400)
GIVEN `the original award does not include an award of the mobility component` IS A BOOLEAN
      `C had a previous award of the mobility component` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day entitlement under the previous award ceased` IS A DATE
      `the date on which the supersession takes or would take effect` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 27(4): entitlement under the previous award is treated as if it were under the original award` MEANS
        `the original award does not include an award of the mobility component`
    AND `C had a previous award of the mobility component`
    AND (`add years` `the day entitlement under the previous award ceased` 1) AT LEAST `the date on which the supersession takes or would take effect`
